+# Private append-media implementation status
+
+Status after129,2026-11-09. This is implementation and compile evidence, not
+Android playback evidence. The historical notes below describe earlier stages;
+their "missing" lists and test counts are not the current status.
+
+## Current implementation
+
+- Bounded incremental fMP4 framing and transactional AVC/AAC extraction,
+  original-mdat payload bounds, pre-allocation fragment count checks, local
+  sample data references, parent-aware init/fragment singleton validation,
+  unique per-track fragment defaults and codec/handler identity checks.
+- Later implicit trun offsets and ignored prefixes preserve original sample
+  positions. One nonnegative-media-time, rate-one edit maps timestamps before
+  endpoint quantization. Complex/empty/negative-time/nonunit edits still reject.
+- Coded-frame storage includes offset/window processing, random-access gating,
+  overlap/dependent-frame replacement, sequence groups, discontinuity handling,
+  track-range intersection, removal, eviction and retained configuration epochs.
+- Private AppendSource/AppendBuffer, AndroidAppendPlayer, bounded worker,
+  decoder-input/output adapters, renderer handoff and AAudio output wiring are
+  implemented. Private DOM wrappers include source/buffer identity, attachment,
+  operations/events, duration/EOS, seek/replay and track-selection epoch guards.
+  Existence of these paths does not establish complete standards conformance.
+
+## Verification and activation are separate
+
+The129 host run passed298 checks (245 unit/native-mock and53 fixture checks).
+These compile the included backend sources with deterministic native symbols,
+not Android codecs or audio hardware. Android owner-source build129 passed:
+https://github.com/vio137/argon/actions/runs/42536136885
+The artifact digest, matching root/deps library CRC+size, exact26Servo+3focus JNI
+exports and onFavicon marker were checked. Compilation does not prove playback.
+
+Both media_android_backend_enabled and dom_media_source_extensions_enabled
+remain false. MediaSource.isTypeSupported remains false. No feature is enabled
+or advertised by these changes, and no delivered APK contains activated media.
+
+Still unverified: actual MediaCodec configure/decode, ImageReader interoperability,
+real decoded video in the renderer, audible AAudio output, device clock/A/V sync,
+browser event behavior under live decoding, and site playback. No emulator/device
+or Firebase tests were run. A real runtime test needs its own permitted scope.
+
+Known format/conformance limits include WebM, inband AVC sample-entry variants,
+brand compatibility validation, broader codec/profile/device support, complex
+edits, encrypted sample support and a full parser/resource/conformance review.
+Recognized unsupported protection layouts reject; that is not DRM support or
+proof that every possible protection layout is detected. Reader/View DOM and
+legacy patches040/041 remain excluded from candidates.
+
+## Dependency and fixture provenance
+
+shiguredo_mp4=2026.5.0, Apache-2.0. Effective dependency MSRV1.93; owner
+compilation uses Rust1.99.1. Registry checksum
+82e773aead88d11a806c8b78dbc2577afb3a20fcc80108aafb3724f6dbb9fbe0,
+source commit30e9b347f8863cd7d377e728ca7a81ac5a1b7770.
+Synthetic local AVC/AAC fMP4 fixtures contain no user media. They prove byte,
+timestamp and mock-boundary behavior, not native decoding.
+Requirements: https://www.w3.org/TR/mse-byte-stream-format-isobmff/
+and https://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaCodec .
+
